cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenTideConstants, cite the release you used by the concept DOI
  (the one DOI for all versions) and the release datestamp (YYYYMMDD). If the
  release has its own Zenodo version, add its version DOI. Also cite the
  upstream data sources of the stations you used
  (see https://opentideconstants.org/about/#attribution).
title: "OpenTideConstants: open tidal harmonic constants"
abstract: >-
  An open dataset of tidal harmonic constants, rebuilt automatically from the
  latest upstream data, with declared conventions and published accuracy for
  every station.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "OpenTideConstants contributors"
url: "https://opentideconstants.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/opentideconstants/opentideconstants"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - tides
  - tidal harmonic constants
  - sea level
  - tide gauges
  - GESLA
# The concept DOI is minted at the first release. Then add it here as doi:
# (the concept DOI, not a version DOI), so this file cites all versions.
